        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: وقود",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وقود — waqūd — \"fuel\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "اشترينا الوقود من محطة صغيرة. ishtaraynā al-waqūd min maḥaṭṭa ṣaghīra. We bought fuel at a small station."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وقود (waqūd) is built on the native Arabic root w-q-d, \"to burn, to blaze\" (Lane). A waqūd is what is burned."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
